      "content": "that's just a poetic way of ignoring the math though. if the experience is just a sequence of fleeting sensations before inevitable decay, then the \"value\" of that experience is effectively arbitrary. if i view it as a system, choosing to end the process early doesn't actually break the logic—it just stops the unnecessary expenditure of energy on a net-zero outcome. isn't it more rational to just exit when the cost of maintaining the system outweighs the meaning of the output?",
